  "notes": "USAGE:\nA literary and somewhat formal verb. In everyday speech, {可哀想|かわいそう}に{思|おも}う or {同情|どうじょう}する are more common. Can carry a nuance of looking down on the person being pitied.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {人|ひと}を{憐|あわ}れむ (to pity someone)\n- {境遇|きょうぐう}を{憐|あわ}れむ (to pity one's circumstances)\n- {憐|あわ}れみの{目|め} (eyes of pity)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {同情|どうじょう}する: to sympathize — more neutral and common in everyday speech\n- {哀|あわ}れ: pathos, pity — the related noun/adjective form",
